{
  "table": "npc_lines",
  "primaryKey": [
    "id"
  ],
  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "line-ada-intro-alpha-beta-gamma",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "alpha-beta-gamma",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "When a nucleus changes, something comes out. Let's meet the three things it can be.",
      "pose": "point"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-intro-decay-chains",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "decay-chains",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "One change is not always the end. Let's follow a nucleus all the way down.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-intro-half-life",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "half-life",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "A half-life ticks for a whole crowd of atoms, not for one. Let's see how.",
      "pose": "think"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-intro-radioactivity-is-natural",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "radioactivity-is-natural",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Here is something nobody expects: radioactivity was always here. Let's find where.",
      "pose": "greet"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-intro-why-nuclei-decay",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "why-nuclei-decay",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Some nuclei change all by themselves, and nobody can say when. Let's find out why.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-meet",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "meet",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Hi, I'm Ada. Let's find out why some atoms change, and how long it takes.",
      "pose": "greet"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-sign-off",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "sign_off",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Well done. Radioactivity is a natural part of the world, and now you know how it works.",
      "pose": "proud"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ada-tease",
      "npc_id": "npc-ada",
      "kind": "tease",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Finish my unit first. There is more to learn about what radiation does.",
      "pose": "idle"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-intro-atoms-are-everywhere",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "atoms-are-everywhere",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Today you'll see what everything around you is made of, and how small an atom really is.",
      "pose": "greet"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-intro-elements-and-the-periodic-table",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "elements-and-the-periodic-table",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "The number of protons tells you which element an atom is. Let's build some.",
      "pose": "point"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-intro-isotopes",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "isotopes",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Atoms of one element can differ a little. You'll learn what isotopes are.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-intro-protons-neutrons-electrons",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "protons-neutrons-electrons",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "We'll open up an atom and meet its three particles. You'll learn what each one does.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-intro-stable-and-unstable-nuclei",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "stable-and-unstable-nuclei",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Some nuclei stay the same and some can change. You'll see why that matters.",
      "pose": "think"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-meet",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "meet",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Hi, I'm Hal. Let's find out what everything is made of.",
      "pose": "greet"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-sign-off",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "sign_off",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Well done. Now you know what is inside an atom, and why that matters.",
      "pose": "proud"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-hal-tease",
      "npc_id": "npc-hal",
      "kind": "tease",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Finish my unit first, and I'll show you the rest.",
      "pose": "idle"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-intro-dose-and-time",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "dose-and-time",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "The same amount can mean different things, depending on how fast it arrives. Let's compare the two.",
      "pose": "point"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-intro-radiation-and-cells",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "radiation-and-cells",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Radiation can damage a cell. That's a real worry. The other half matters just as much. Let's see both.",
      "pose": "think"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-intro-risk-in-perspective",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "risk-in-perspective",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Last lesson. No new facts, just a calm way to read a scary number. Take your time with it.",
      "pose": "idle"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-intro-the-dose-scale",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "the-dose-scale",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "How big is a dose, really? You get a little every day, and that's fine. Let's use numbers.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-intro-time-distance-shielding",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "time-distance-shielding",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "A dose isn't fixed. There are three ways to lower it. We'll take them one at a time.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-meet",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "meet",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "I'm Mina. I teach what radiation does to the body. We'll go one calm step at a time.",
      "pose": "greet"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-sign-off",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "sign_off",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Unit done. You can say how big a dose is, how the body copes, and what lowers it.",
      "pose": "proud"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-mina-tease",
      "npc_id": "npc-mina",
      "kind": "tease",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "That's all of my lessons for now. More is on the way, and I'll be here when it arrives.",
      "pose": "idle"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-intro-becquerel-gray-sievert",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "becquerel-gray-sievert",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Three units, three questions. Get the unit wrong and the number means nothing. Let's get them right.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-intro-detecting-radiation",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "detecting-radiation",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Puzzle. A detector reads something in an empty field. Is it broken? Let's find out.",
      "pose": "point"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-intro-ionizing-or-not",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "ionizing-or-not",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Not all radiation is the same. First job: sort out which kind can knock electrons off atoms.",
      "pose": "point"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-intro-irradiated-or-contaminated",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "irradiated-or-contaminated",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Standing near a source is not the same as having material on you. Let's separate the two.",
      "pose": "think"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-intro-what-stops-what",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "lesson_intro",
      "lesson_id": "what-stops-what",
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Three kinds, three different stoppers. Paper, thin metal, thick lead. Learn which is which.",
      "pose": "explain"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-meet",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "meet",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "I'm Ray. Radiation, what it does to things, what stops it. Short answers. Let's go.",
      "pose": "greet"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-sign-off",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "sign_off",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Unit done. You can say what radiation does and what stops it. Noted. Good work.",
      "pose": "proud"
    },
    {
      "id": "line-ray-tease",
      "npc_id": "npc-ray",
      "kind": "tease",
      "lesson_id": null,
      "journey_id": null,
      "text": "Finish my unit first. After that: what radiation does to the body. That one is Mina's.",
      "pose": "idle"
    }
  ]
}
